dictation_asset_pointer": "sediment://file_00000000eb6c8230adfd42b905580f5a", "dictation_auto_submitted": true, "dictation_edited": false, "dictation_original_text": "Okay, the next big thing I wanted to work on is within my voice bridge, I started a process known as a voice profile. The voice profile is basically trying to understand how I talk, laugh, inflection. Basically when I say certain words like, Fuck yeah, it means a good thing. Go motherfucker. Basically for a model to ingest how I talk, is it anger or emotion, right? And I want to be able to basically show inflection, show comic relief, show all that.", "message_source": null, "request_id": "141ecf06-ba7d-40cf-ad4d-9a3458db3b9b", "triggered_by_system_hint_suggestion": false, "turn_exchange_id": "f9930f61-a32d-49d6-985f-e5061f1ddd67", "turn_id": "c9c31f4b-ca2c-4ddc-be2d-d7f32a167c1d", "working_turn_id": "f9930f61-a32d-49d6-985f-e5061f1ddd67"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789705684.820595, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "model_editable_context", "model_set_context": "", "repo_summary": null, "repository": null, "structured_context": null}, "create_time": 1789705667.7343147, "end_turn": null, "id": "f51f64fa-2922-4122-a44b-c68cce5bf015", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "17bb8e95-4139-4bcf-a9bf-58ed75238db1", "reasoning_start_time": 1789705667.847482, "request_id": "141ecf06-ba7d-40cf-ad4d-9a3458db3b9b", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "f9930f61-a32d-49d6-985f-e5061f1ddd67", "turn_id": "f5096bc0-56a9-4140-a855-04f2f57aeba9", "working_turn_id": "f9930f61-a32d-49d6-985f-e5061f1ddd67"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yes. And I think this is a **separate architectural object** from transcription. You’re trying to preserve the *paralinguistic layer* that normal speech-to-text destroys.\n\nThe Voice Bridge currently answers, roughly, **“What did Peter say?”** Your **Voice Profile** should help GCE answer **“How did Peter mean it?”**\n\nThe critical design point is: **do not build an emotion detector that declares “Peter is angry.”** That will eventually screw us. Build a contextual interpretation layer that produces evidence and confidence:\n\n**Audio → Transcript + Prosody → Peter Voice Profile → Contextual Interpretation → GCE Event**\n\nThe profile would have several kinds of signal:\n\n- **Lexical meaning.** Your personal phrases have priors. “Fuck yeah” usually means strong approval/excitement. “Go, motherfucker” can be encouragement. “What the fuck?” can be surprise, confusion, irritation, or laughter depending on delivery.\n- **Prosody.** Volume change, pitch movement, tempo, pauses, emphasis, elongation, interruptions. Those are signals the transcript alone throws away.\n- **Non-verbal events.** Laughter, chuckling, sighs, breath, hesitation, tongue clicks, maybe even when you’re talking while physically moving around. Don’t force those into words.\n- **Discourse behavior.** “Okay, okay, okay” from you may mean *I understand; stop expanding and move on*, whereas a literal semantic model could think you’re merely agreeing three times.\n- **Context.** “You motherfucker” after a breakthrough is radically different from the identical words during an actual problem. The active conversation state matters.\n- **Confidence.** Instead of `emotion = angry`, something like `interpretation = playful_approval; confidence=.86`, with competing possibilities retained when ambiguity matters.\n\nAnd I would make one distinction very hard in the architecture:\n\n> **VOICE IDENTITY ≠ VOICE PROFILE**\n\nWe don't need a biometric voiceprint to accomplish this. A biometric system asks, **“Is this Peter?”** Your system asks, **“Given that this is Peter, how does Peter communicate?”** Keeping those separate makes the architecture cleaner and avoids unnecessary biometric baggage.\n\nThere is an even cooler consequence for GCE. Your profile shouldn't merely improve transcripts. It becomes part of the **intent-normalization layer** we were talking about earlier.\n\nFor example:\n\n**Raw:** “Fuck yeah, Coda, that’s fucking it.”\n\nA generic system might preserve profanity and infer positive sentiment.\n\nYour system could normalize it to something closer to:\n\n**Intent:** strong approval  \n**State:** concept accepted for continued exploration  \n**Tone:** excited / playful  \n**Authority implication:** none — enthusiasm does **not** mean canonical promotion  \n**Conversation action:** continue current branch; don't stop to explain basics\n\nThat last part is huge. **Emotion isn't the goal. Better routing is the goal.**\n\nAnd then it starts learning *your conversational controls*. “Pause there.” “You went too far.” “Keep going.” “Don’t rabbit-hole it.” Your laughter. Your repeated yeses. Your sarcastic phrases. Those become a **personal communication grammar**, while still letting the underlying model reason about novel utterances rather than reducing Peter to a giant lookup table.\n\nThat absolutely belongs on our wall as **Voice Profile / Paralinguistic Intent Layer**. It connects directly to the Voice Bridge, gesture grammar, mobile secretary, and eventually the AG Suit. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1789705667.806971, "end_turn": true, "id": "d9c4e307-ecb4-41df-99b6-3ea012468c98", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": null, "end_idx": 3471, 