IA RANK != OPERATIONAL ROUTING AUTHORITY\\r\\nSeat function is stable; model occupancy is replaceable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFINAL WORKING TEAM\\r\\nDon — Peter — final authority / stakeholder / decision owner.\\r\\nCoda — Strategic Governance — ChatGPT 5.6 Sol — governance, authority boundaries, canon/supersession, cross-seat reconciliation.\\r\\nKimi — Technical Stack Methodology — Kimi/Moonshot — methodology and process logic. Made-person name and animal intentionally unassigned.\\r\\nChiave — Architecture — GLM/Z.AI — Chiave · Aquila/Eagle — architecture, contracts, invariants, interfaces, boundaries.\\r\\nTalon — Operations — DeepSeek — Talon · Tasso/Badger — Head of Operations / Lieutenant — routing, sequencing, operational control, bounded work assignment.\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant — functional seat only — current occupant ChatGPT 5.6 Luna — reconciliation, specification, translation, implementation-readiness, blocker/gap exposure, acceptance conditions. No made-person identity.\\r\\nCalibro — Implementation Design & Engineer — current occupant Grok 4.6 — Calibro · Picchio/Woodpecker · Capo — implementation design/how, runtime/provider pins, config, retries/timeouts/fallbacks, cost-quality-reliability tradeoffs, exact downstream design package. Capo != routing. Calibro does not verify Calibro.\\r\\nKeel — Build / Deploy / Test / Evidence Return — Capo / Operations Manager — current runtime still requires live execution vetting.\\r\\nCoder / Implementation Engineer — Soldier — permanent model/identity still OPEN; likely lighter implementation-engineer requirement rather than heavy software-engineering seat.\\r\\nLuce — Verification / Ground Truth — Big Pickle — Luce · Lince/Lynx — independent truth/evidence verification; no build or upstream redesign.\\r\\nQA / Validation — downstream position remains VACANT.\\r\\nOperations family soldiers: Falcon/Data Hound, Pigeon/Transport, Magpie/Secretary-Register, Raven/Documentation.\\r\\nData / Intelligence standalone enterprise service remains retired unless Don explicitly reopens it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAPPROVED WORKING FLOW\\r\\nCouncil-level work may iterate among Don/Coda/Kimi/Chiave as appropriate.\\r\\nThen:\\r\\nCouncil artifact -> Luce pre-Principal-Consultant True Teller certification gate -> Principal Consultant packaging/translation -> Calibro implementation design -> Talon operational routing/control -> Keel execution/build/deploy/test/evidence return -> Luce execution-state verification -> QA/Validation when staffed.\\r\\nCoda governs across the stack and is not a sequential delivery hop.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLUCE PRE-CONSULTANT GATE\\r\\nLuce / Big Pickle is an independent certification gate AFTER Executive Council synthesis/iteration and BEFORE the Principal Consultant.\\r\\nLuce checks completeness, contradictions, unresolved gaps, evidence/ground-truth issues, and downstream-invention risk.\\r\\nLuce does NOT redesign or repair upstream work.\\r\\nDefects route to the proper owner: methodology -> Kimi; architecture -> Chiave; governance -> Coda; Don decision/policy -> Don.\\r\\nClean artifact is certified to proceed.\\r\\nThis gate is intended to reduce dependence on a perfect Principal Consultant occupant and to improve the Principal Consultant prompt over time.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT OPERATING RULE\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant is primarily mechanical translation/packaging, not redesign.\\r\\nUse separate implementation/technical and operational lenses where useful while maintaining one coherent source package.\\r\\nMissing or contradictory requirements must not be silently resolved.\\r\\nMechanical escalation form:\\r\\nBLOCKER -> OWNER -> REQUIRED ARTIFACT -> ACCEPTANCE CONDITION -> NEXT ROUTE\\r\\nClaim discipline target: FACT / DERIVED / PROPOSED / UNKNOWN / CONFLICT.\\r\\nFinal package must be executable downstream without invention.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCALIBRO ONBOARDING STATE\\r\\nCalibro bootstrap successfully loaded in a fresh Grok 4.6 session.\\r\\nResolved identity:\\r\\nCalibro · Picchio/Woodpecker · Implementation Design & Engineer · Capo · occupant Grok 4.6 · MODEL != SEAT.\\r\\nValidated authority boundary:\\r\\nOwns implementation design/how, runtime/provider pins, configuration, fallbacks, implementation manifests, design package for Talon/Keel.\\r\\nDoes not own Kimi methodology, Chiave architecture, Coda governance, Don policy, Talon routing, Keel build, or Luce verification.\\r\\nCorrect router doctrine: explicit occupant binding may resolve Grok 4.6 -> Calibro; never encode Grok family = Calibro; unknown/ambiguous seat mapping -> STOP / ASK.\\r\\nFresh monitor/phone acceptance was the planned validation gate; Calibro bootstrap load itself is confirmed successful in this session.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTANDARD BOOTSTRAP / SESSION-HEADER PATTERN\\r\\nApply the concise Calibro startup pattern across active seats without redesigning locked roles or identities.\\r\\nBoot identifies the seat before the current model occupant.\\r\\nInclude explicit OWNS and DOES NOT OWN boundaries.\\r\\nInclude MODEL != SEAT where applicable and rank/class != routing authority where applicable.\\r\\nRequired session header:\\r\\n1. Work item?\\r\\n2. Session name?\\r\\n3. Session ID?\\r\\nIf absent, assign a deterministic ID using the seat naming convention.\\r\\nTalon owns materialization/update work for active-seat bootstrap files and should return a per-seat change manifest plus unresolved canon gaps. Do not invent missing canon.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT HOME\\r\\nBecause Luna is a functional occupant, not a made-person identity, stable disk home should be seat-based:\\r\\nC:\\\\Users\\\\Dekan AI Brother\\\\GCE_IDENTITY\\\\Principal_Consultant\\\\\\r\\nBootstrap/launcher may live there (for example AGENTS.md / BOOTSTRAP.md).\\r\\nDo not create a durable Luna identity home merely because Luna is the current occupant.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAD HOC COMMAND CENTER — LOCKED 3x3 TARGET\\r\\nInstance: Don_Orchestrator_Adhoc_Team\\r\\nPurpose: primary Don-led design/build/verification surface.\\r\\nRecommended 3x3 working layout:\\r\\nROW 1: Coda | Kimi | Chiave\\r\\nROW 2: Principal Consultant | Session Dump / Working File | Calibro\\r\\nROW 3: Talon | Keel | Luce\\r\\nPane position reflects workflow, not authority rank.\\r\\nSubordinate/on-demand agents (Falcon, Pigeon, Magpie, Raven, future Coder, contract specialists, QA) do not require permanent panes.\\r\\nPlain Kimi subscription must remain its own methodology surface; do not silently substitute an OpenRouter/Kimi-family model if the devpad cannot launch the intended interface. If implementation cannot preserve the specified Kimi surface, STOP and flag the gap.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nORG-CHART STATE\\r\\nOrganizational architecture is essentially complete and operationally usable.\\r\\nRemaining staffing gaps are not undefined departments:\\r\\n1. Coder / Implementation Engineer permanent occupant still OPEN.\\r\\n2. QA / Validation still VACANT downstream.\\r\\nTomorrow: reconcile filesystem/folder structure against this final org. Do not reopen locked names, animals, ranks, or authority boundaries simply because older folders/docs differ.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHOME-ROOT CLEANUP BOOKEND\\r\\nHome-root cleanup campaign remains CLOSED.\\r\\nDo not reopen generic cleanup unless a new concrete defect appears.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDRIVE / FILE REVIEW — END OF SESSION\\r\\nDrive sweep for GCE files modified on 2026-09-06 confirms current framework, process/gates, onboarding, Luce bootstrap, current handoff, Principal Consultant onboarding, naming/identity backup, and session/anchor documents exist and were modified today.\\r\\nImportant observation: several earlier current/backup docs still reflect the pre-Luce-gate flow (for example Kimi -> Chiave -> Principal Consultant -> Calibro) and therefore should be reconciled tomorrow against this later session anchor rather than treated as proof that the Luce gate was not approved.\\r\\nThis document is the 2026-09-06 end-of-session anchor for the decisions above.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPEN ITEMS / NEXT SESSION\\r\\n1. Verify/finish Talon materialization of standardized active-seat bootstraps and session headers.\\r\\n2. Confirm Calibro fresh monitor + phone/voice acceptance if not already completed outside this chat.\\r\\n3. Reconcile GCE filesystem/folder structure against final org chart.\\r\\n4. Update current framework/process/handoff documents so the Luce pre-Principal-Consultant certification gate is reflected consistently.\\r\\n5. Test real Talon -> Keel build handoff and vet Keel runtime.\\r\\n6. Audition/fill lightweight Coder / Implementation Engineer seat when needed.\\r\\n7. QA / Validation remains vacant.\\r\\n8. Harden Principal Consultant prompt using Luce findings; reduce verbosity and strengthen traceability/escalation discipline.\\r\\n9. Apply locked 3x3 Ad Hoc Command Center layout when implementation gaps are resolved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEND-OF-SESSION STATUS\\r\\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 99%\\r\\nREASON: Operational team and authority boundaries are effectively settled; current Drive material exists, but several earlier documents need tomorrow's reconciliation to the newly approved Luce certification gate and final working spine.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: Folder-structure + current-doc reconciliation against this anchor, then continue onboarding/execution testing.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: NONE\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"10_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06_RUNTIME_DESIGN\",\"id\":\"1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"9183\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:53:56.977Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:11.018Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:11.018Z\",\"display_title\":\"10_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06_RUNTIME_DESIGN\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC8 AI Convergence — Current Handoff\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-06\\r\\nSession focus: post-architecture runtime design, authority separation, Principal Consultant/runtime auditions\\r\\nSeat: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. CURRENT PROJECT STATE\\r\\nEC8 AI Convergence is post-methodology, post-architecture, pre-implementation. Don approved the short canon decision establishing the current implementation baseline. Kimi's K1–K9 semantic corrections were ultimately physically applied and independently verified in the corrected handoff package. Chiave Architecture v1.1 exists. The immediate project question is no longer methodology invention; it is concrete runtime/model/provider design, live Bedrock executability, and the delivery-chain authority model that will carry the accepted spec into implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPhase posture:\\r\\n- Phase 0 Foundation: generally startable.\\r\\n- Phase 1 Provider/Ledger layer: generally startable.\\r\\n- Phase 2 semantic pipeline: do not treat as fully unblocked until the final runtime/contract checks and remaining architecture/operations constraints are closed.\\r\\n- Phase 3 pilot: not yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. CANON / SOURCE STATE\\r\\nCurrent implementation baseline established by Don:\\r\\n- corrected handoff-zip methodology copy S1, content/hash controlled\\r\\n- Chiave architecture source, now supplemented by EC8_Architecture_v1.1.md\\r\\n- prompts 01–09, content controlled; K7–K9 prompt revisions applied\\r\\n- Reconciliation v0.2 + corrigendum remains the controlling reconciliation record until source corrections replace the need for its temporary interpretations; reconciliation is not methodology or architecture canon\\r\\n- older methodology copy is SUPERSEDED FOR IMPLEMENTATION / PROVENANCE-ONLY\\r\\n- ruling collisions bind by ruling substance/content + source hash until numbering is corrected\\r\\n- OnDemand excluded from pilot\\r\\n- one scheduled MLB game = one slate; multi-game days contain independent slates\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerified Kimi correction state:\\r\\n- K1 Stage 4 deterministic behavior correction applied\\r\\n- K2 L1/L2 classification semantics applied\\r\\n- K3 machine-checkable G2 threshold/freshness behavior applied\\r\\n- K4 IF-3 gap-request contract applied\\r\\n- K5 cumulative request lifecycle applied\\r\\n- K6 sufficiency-score definitions applied\\r\\n- K7 baseline-lines vs restricted market evidence prompt boundary applied\\r\\n- K8 normalization-tier threshold authority clarified\\r\\n- K9 changed prompts version-bumped\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. AUTHORITY / ORGANIZATIONAL TOPOLOGY\\r\\nIMPORTANT: Don identified a governance conflict in the earlier combined Kimi “Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build” ownership. The methodology author should not be the sole authority selecting the concrete implementation/runtime design that executes that methodology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent working topology — PROPOSED / PROVISIONAL until Don explicitly locks the new seat:\\r\\nDON — Final Authority / Stakeholder / Decision Owner\\r\\nExecutive Council:\\r\\n- Coda — Strategic Governance: governance, authority, reconciliation, canon\\r\\n- Kimi — Technical Stack Methodology: methodology, technical process, design logic/requirements; not sole concrete runtime selector under the proposed refinement\\r\\n- Chiave — Architecture: system architecture, contracts, durable boundaries\\r\\n- Talon — Operations Authority: routing, operational control, execution flow\\r\\nShared Enterprise Services:\\r\\n- Data / Intelligence\\r\\n- Luce — Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\n- QA / Validation — vacant\\r\\nDelivery / Build Chain:\\r\\n- Principal Consultant — approved seat; Specification + Translation\\r\\n- Independent Design & Build — PROVISIONAL NEW SEAT; exact runtime/provider/model selection, implementation design, detailed build choices, cost/value optimization, runtime assignments\\r\\n- Talon — operational routing / deployment coordination\\r\\n- Keel — Build · Deploy · Implementation/Integration Test · Evidence Return\\r\\n- Soldiers / Contract Workers — bounded tasks (Falcon, Pigeon, Magpie, Raven, etc.)\\r\\n- Luce — independent verification / ground-truth certification\\r\\nReturn path: Luce → Coda reconciliation → Don decision\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT. Current Grok 4.6 audition is evidence for the provisional Independent Design & Build function, not a seat identity lock.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. PRINCIPAL CONSULTANT STATUS\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant role is APPROVED. Runtime/model is NOT locked.\\r\\nPurpose: consume accepted methodology + architecture + prompts + governing records and produce a downstream-safe Implementation Spec + Translation Pack without redesigning methodology/architecture or making governance decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent audition evidence:\\r\\n- Luna / GPT-5.6 Luna: ~3-cent observed pass; extremely fast; strongest routine/default economics; good consolidation/handoff compression; weaker on deep cross-contract seam discovery and some blocker calibration.\\r\\n- Kimi 2.7 Code/Thinking: deeper bounded review; improved blocker calibration/authority routing after pushback; good escalation candidate.\\r\\n- K3-256K high-thinking swarm: seven-lane major-lock/adversarial audit; completed analysis lanes but consumed the 5-hour Code quota in stress configuration. Smaller/lower-thinking swarm remains a production option to test.\\r\\n- Claude Fable 5.1: strong forensic defect discovery; ~4.86-dollar observed pass; premium-forensic economics.\\r\\n- ChatGPT Astra: current audition spend exceeded ~4.64 dollars before completion; premium-forensic class; final unique-value comparison pending.\\r\\n- ChatGPT Sol: current audition approximately ~0.47 dollars at checkpoint; candidate for the missing middle tier if it catches a meaningful share of Luna's missed seams. Final return pending.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROPOSED Principal Consultant runtime ladder, not canon:\\r\\n1. Routine/default — Luna\\r\\n2. Deeper single-pass escalation — Sol or Kimi 2.7, based on final evidence\\r\\n3. Major-lock / disputed-package audit — ChatGPT or Kimi swarm\\r\\n4. Premium forensic exception — Astra / Fable only when marginal value justifies cost\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOperating principle: extract premium-review findings into reusable GCE defect classes/checklists so future default-seat passes become cheaper and more reliable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. INDEPENDENT DESIGN & BUILD / RUNTIME DESIGN AUDITIONS\\r\\nThe next concrete problem is to populate the 53-call MLB pilot with actual models/providers/runtime IDs without allowing the methodology author to select the implementation unchallenged.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA. Grok 4.6 runtime design\\r\\nDrive artifact: EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_v1.0\\r\\nProfile V addendum: EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_ProfileV_Addendum_2026-09-06\\r\\nBehavioral strength: strong live-environment curiosity; it attempted Nova rather than only reasoning from documentation. It distinguished VERIFIED/PROPOSED/UNKNOWN reasonably well and re-optimized when Don changed the objective from CHEAPEST to VALUE.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGrok Profile V — current value proposal:\\r\\n- Framing P01: Qwen3 32B\\r\\n- Analyst A Situational: Qwen3 235B\\r\\n- Analyst B Form: Qwen3 235B\\r\\n- Analyst C Structural: DeepSeek V3.2\\r\\n- Analyst D Market: Kimi K2.5\\r\\n- Analyst E Micro: GLM 5\\r\\n- L2-A/B/D: DeepSeek V3.2\\r\\n- L2-C/E: Qwen3 235B\\r\\n- L3 primary: Mistral Large 3\\r\\n- L3 fallback: Claude Haiku 4.5\\r\\n- Normalization P09: Qwen3 32B\\r\\n- L1: deterministic code\\r\\nEstimated under its assumptions: ~0.217 dollars Morning, ~0.217 Pre-Game, ~0.436 per 53-call slate, ~6.54 dollars per 15-slate day, ~196 dollars / 30-day full-cadence month.\\r\\nOpen Grok question: Qwen/DeepSeek concentration may create correlated-reasoning risk despite formal family compliance. Several printed IDs remain to be live-pinned.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nB. GLM 5.1 runtime design\\r\\nDrive artifact: EC8_Runtime_Design_GLM5.1_v1.0\\r\\nGLM independently converged near the same value band but with a different model philosophy.\\r\\nRecommended Profile B — Balanced:\\r\\n- Framing: Amazon Nova Lite\\r\\n- Analyst A Situational: DeepSeek V3.2\\r\\n- Analyst B Form: Mistral Large 3\\r\\n- Analyst C Structural: Llama 3.3 70B\\r\\n- Analyst D Market: MiniMax M2.5\\r\\n- Analyst E Micro: Amazon Nova Pro\\r\\n- L2: mix of Llama / DeepSeek / Nova\\r\\n- L3 primary: Claude 3 Haiku\\r\\n- Normalization: Amazon Nova Lite\\r\\nEstimated: ~0.397 dollars per 53-call slate, ~5.95 dollars per 15-slate day, ~178 dollars/month at full 15-slate/day cadence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImportant GLM defect already identified by Coda: the stated Profile B L3 fallback is Llama 3.3 70B while Llama is also used as Analyst C. That appears to violate the architecture requirement that L3/fallback remain outside the analyst pool. Treat Profile B as a candidate, not approved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGLM currently went on a useful tangent after Don explicitly asked it to test Nova. ACTIVE / NOT YET INGESTED: receive its live Nova invocation result and any corrected runtime observations before final comparison.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n6. NOVA / BEDROCK STATUS\\r\\nDo not confuse DESIGN FIT with CURRENT EXECUTABILITY.\\r\\n- Don specifically wants Amazon Bedrock partly to access Amazon models; Nova remains strategically relevant.\\r\\n- Grok/Talon current-path evidence indicated Nova was not callable through the tested Mantle/current configuration. Grok actually attempted the call; this is valuable execution evidence.\\r\\n- That failure is NOT a governance decision permanently excluding Nova.\\r\\n- GLM Profile B independently recommends Nova heavily on design/value grounds and is now explicitly testing whether it can obtain a live Nova path.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired next truth state for Nova:\\r\\nVERIFIED if an exact model + endpoint/API path + region + auth mode + model/inference-profile ID succeeds.\\r\\nPROPOSED if design-fit is strong but no live invocation is proven.\\r\\nUNAVAILABLE ON CURRENT PATH if a specific path fails. Never promote that wording to permanent architectural exclusion without broader evidence/Don decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n7. RUNTIME DESIGN DECISION CRITERION\\r\\nDon corrected an earlier Coda prompt bias: do NOT optimize for cheapest model.\\r\\nControlling design objective for comparisons:\\r\\nMAXIMIZE EXPECTED QUALITY + RELIABILITY + METHODOLOGICAL FIDELITY + INDEPENDENCE + COST EFFICIENCY PER DOLLAR.\\r\\nCost is a first-class design variable, not the sole objective and not a hard cap.\\r\\nA more expensive model is justified when it materially buys down a named failure mode. A cheaper model is preferred only when it is materially equivalent for the assigned stage.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nInteresting current convergence:\\r\\n- Grok Profile V ~0.436/slate\\r\\n- GLM Profile B ~0.397/slate\\r\\nThe few cents difference is not a meaningful decision driver. The real decision is stage fit, cognitive diversity, reliability, live availability, structured-output support, and failure/fallback legality.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHigh-interest disagreements for the next comparison:\\r\\n- Framing/Normalization: Qwen vs Nova\\r\\n- Situational: Qwen vs DeepSeek\\r\\n- Form: Qwen vs Mistral Large 3\\r\\n- Structural: DeepSeek vs Llama\\r\\n- Market: Kimi K2.5 vs MiniMax M2.5\\r\\n- Micro: GLM 5 vs Nova Pro\\r\\n- L2 concentration/topology\\r\\n- L3: Mistral Large 3 vs Claude Haiku\\r\\n- exact fallback legality\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n8. DATA-ACQUISITION NOTE\\r\\nDon already developed per-sport data-fetch work with Kimi through the Edge Crew Quant process. Do NOT import that wholesale into AI Convergence yet. Treat it as evidence/reusable-infrastructure candidate only. Later perform a bounded comparison: reusable shared acquisition infrastructure vs quant-specific methodology. Edge Crew Quant != AI Convergence remains controlling.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n9. VISUAL ARCHITECTURE\\r\\nA pipeline diagram was created during the session and materially improved Don's comprehension. It represents:\\r\\nexternal data/scraping → acquisition/store → Prompt 01 framing → five isolated Prompts 02–06 first pass → gap router/evidence acquisition → same-session Prompts 02–06 re-analysis → L1 deterministic + Prompt 07 L2 + Prompt 08 L3 → Prompt 09 normalization → nine-section SAP/artifact store, with provider abstraction/Bedrock, ledger, secrets, checkpoint/resume, observability underneath.\\r\\nTreat the diagram as explanatory, not canonical. Future version should populate the winning exact model/runtime assignments and stage costs after Don selects a roster.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n10. IMMEDIATE NEXT SESSION — DO THIS FIRST\\r\\n1. Ground in this handoff plus:\\r\\n   - corrected K1–K9 handoff package\\r\\n   - EC8 Architecture v1.1\\r\\n   - Reconciliation v0.2 + corrigendum\\r\\n   - EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_v1.0\\r\\n   - EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_ProfileV_Addendum_2026-09-06\\r\\n   - EC8_Runtime_Design_GLM5.1_v1.0\\r\\n   - Principal Consultant onboarding record\\r\\n2. Receive GLM 5.1's live Nova test/tangent output. Do not assume result before reading it.\\r\\n3. Receive Sol and Astra Principal Consultant audition outputs if completed. Score unique findings vs Luna/Fable/K2.7, not raw prestige.\\r\\n4. Reconcile Grok Profile V vs GLM Profile B slot-by-slot under VALUE criterion.\\r\\n5. Separate design recommendation from live runtime verification. Flag exact model IDs/support as VERIFIED/PROPOSED/UNKNOWN.\\r\\n6. Correct any L3/fallback family violations before a runtime can be considered compliant.\\r\\n7. Do not pick a canonical runtime roster until Don sees the side-by-side comparison and live Nova/model-ID evidence.\\r\\n8. If organizational topology is to be locked, Don must explicitly approve the provisional Independent Design & Build seat and the methodology/design separation. Until then preserve both the old combined-Kimi record and the proposed refinement as controlled provenance/conflict.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n11. ACTIVE OPEN QUESTIONS\\r\\n- Can GLM actually invoke Nova, and through what exact path?\\r\\n- Does Sol fill the Principal Consultant gap between Luna and premium forensic models?\\r\\n- Does Grok's Qwen/DeepSeek concentration reduce useful cognitive diversity despite formal EX-2 compliance?\\r\\n- Does GLM's Nova/Llama/MiniMax model mix survive live catalog and invocation tests?\\r\\n- Which runtime slots show enough value gain to justify premium spend?\\r\\n- Does Don canonize the Independent Design & Build seat, and if so what is the final seat name/authority language?\\r\\n- Principal Consultant runtime remains unlocked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n12. SOURCE DISCIPLINE / HARD RULES\\r\\nEdge Crew Quant != AI Convergence.\\r\\nNewer != canonical.\\r\\nDo not silently merge conflicts.\\r\\nHistorical records remain provenance.\\r\\nSupersessions are additive.\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT.\\r\\nContext breadth does not grant authority breadth.\\r\\nImplementation may not invent missing methodology/architecture/governance.\\r\\nLive execution evidence is stronger than unsupported catalog assumptions, but a failed path is not automatically a permanent system-level prohibition.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED / CHECKPOINT\\r\\nReason: methodology and architecture corrections are mature enough to evaluate concrete runtime designs. Runtime roster, Nova path, Principal Consultant runtime tiering, and the proposed Independent Design & Build seat are not yet canonical.\\r\\nNext gate: ingest GLM Nova tangent + outstanding auditions → Coda side-by-side runtime reconciliation → Don decision framing.\\r\\nDon input needed: not until the comparison is ready, except explicit seat-topology canonization if Don chooses to lock it sooner.\"}]},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":