ull, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content": "Worked for 7s", "content_type": "reasoning_recap"}, "create_time": 1789707290.446708, "end_turn": false, "id": "97615442-04e9-42ac-aee9-376a97806ec1", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 7, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "5ded882b-41ad-460b-8424-b7cf6d3d44c8", "reasoning_end_time": 1789707290.4427269, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1789707282.939024, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "df2a9e57-c3bd-483a-8ca7-8617da56de9e", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "9ba346f0-5c94-4bd6-8897-b617a0fafef6", "turn_id": "e645c2a9-28f3-4f12-bda6-34adac3bbb98", "working_turn_id": "9ba346f0-5c94-4bd6-8897-b617a0fafef6"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "multimodal_text", "parts": [{"asset_pointer": "sediment://file_0000000008e081fd85fa91934f89c60b", "content_type": "image_asset_pointer", "fovea": null, "height": 2048, "metadata": {"asset_pointer_link": null, "container_pixel_height": null, "container_pixel_width": null, "dalle": null, "emu_omit_glimpse_image": null, "emu_patches_override": null, "generation": null, "gizmo": null, "is_no_auth_placeholder": null, "lpe_delta_encoding_channel": null, "lpe_keep_patch_ijhw": null, "sanitized": true, "segmentation": null, "watermarked_asset_pointer": null}, "size_bytes": 169171, "width": 1880}, "Okay, we got a good proof of concept. Take a deep dive at these screenshots. The biggest thing is we have the identity, but it's loading all open code. And your own window at the top left isn't calling up the ChatGPT login for my subscription.  "]}, "create_time": 1789709084.142, "end_turn": null, "id": "af0d4c84-8e5c-4b32-886e-1a25ee10b35f", "metadata": {"attachments": [{"height": 2048, "id": "file_0000000008e081fd85fa91934f89c60b", "is_big_paste": false, "library_file_id": "libfile_98b570e202b081919beacf44f645104d", "mime_type": "image/png", "name": "5fc62f06-6634-42a4-9aa2-4583c420c754.png", "size": 169171, "source": "local", "width": 1880}], "can_save": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "62066f6f-15f5-421b-97d3-23bc7b59c6a6", "selected_sources": [], "serialization_metadata": {"custom_symbol_offsets": []}, "turn_exchange_id": "1fed9948-ee47-4993-9695-072675f61d2e", "turn_id": "e7fbd08b-cdef-4ea0-b047-0886a7ab9080", "working_turn_id": "1fed9948-ee47-4993-9695-072675f61d2e"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789709121.86733, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yeah — this screenshot is actually a very useful proof-of-concept because it shows exactly where the abstraction is still wrong.\n\nWhat’s working is the **seat layer**. The board knows `Coda`, `Corrado`, `Chiave`, `Ragno`, `Calibro`, `Talon`, `Keel`, `Luce`, and the VoiceBridge center tile. That is a real success. The identity homes are also visibly landing in the right places at the bottom of each OpenCode pane, e.g. `GCE_IDENTITY\\Corrado`, `...\\Ragno`, etc.\n\nWhat is **not** working yet is the next layer down: **surface/host resolution**.\n\nRight now, the Command Center appears to be doing something conceptually like:\n\n`seat -> OpenCode`\n\nfor almost every AI seat.\n\nWhat we actually need is:\n\n`seat -> host/surface -> provider/runtime -> model/config`\n\nSo the registry needs to distinguish these things cleanly.\n\nFor example:\n\n| Seat | Surface/Host | Runtime/Provider | Current model |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Coda | **Brave browser window** | ChatGPT subscription | GPT-5.6 Sol |\n| Corrado | OpenCode | Kimi/Moonshot | K3-256K low |\n| Chiave | OpenCode | whatever current Architecture occupant is | configured separately |\n| Ragno | OpenCode | Kimi/Moonshot | Kimi 2.8 Preview |\n| VoiceBridge | Native/local service tile | AssemblyAI + bridge | n/a |\n| Calibro | OpenCode | current Calibro occupant | configured separately |\n| Talon | OpenCode | current Talon occupant | configured separately |\n| Keel | OpenCode | current Keel occupant | configured separately |\n| Luce | OpenCode | Big Pickle/current verifier runtime | configured separately |\n\nSo there’s an important nuance: **OpenCode everywhere is not inherently wrong** if OpenCode is genuinely the host for those seats. What’s wrong is treating OpenCode as the universal seat implementation.\n\n### The top-left Coda failure\n\nThe blank top-left with the broken-page icon is a different problem.\n\nYour board is trying to make **ChatGPT-in-Brave behave like an embeddable web pane**. That is likely the wrong primitive.\n\nYour actual requirement is:\n\n> Open the authenticated ChatGPT subscription session that already lives in Peter’s Brave profile and bind that browser window to the Coda seat.\n\nThat is **not the same thing as loading `chatgpt.com` inside an iframe in DevPad**.\n\nThe screenshot strongly suggests the current implementation is attempting an embedded/docked webpage. Sites like ChatGPT can restrict framing/embedding through browser security policies, and even if we got past that, we would still be fighting session/auth/profile behavior.\n\nFor the first real version, I would not fight the browser.\n\nHave the Coda tile act as a **controller for a real Brave window**:\n\n**Coda tile → launch/focus registered Brave process/window → Peter’s normal Brave profile → authenticated ChatGPT subscription**\n\nThat solves your login problem naturally because the authentication belongs to your existing Brave profile. We do not create a second login/session inside DevPad.\n\nAnd it aligns perfectly with what we said earlier:\n\n> **The pane is not the seat. The pane is the control surface for the seat.**\n\nSo Coda’s tile can initially show something like:\n\n**CODA**  \n`Brave — CONNECTED`  \n`ChatGPT — authenticated`  \n`Window — 0x123ABC`  \n`[Focus] [Restart]`\n\nClicking/focusing it brings your actual Coda browser window forward.\n\nLater, if we decide that physically embedding that surface inside the 3×3 is important enough, then we can investigate a native shell/WebView-style implementation. I would **not make that the blocker now**.\n\n### What the screenshot tells me to build next\n\nI would tell Talon **do not touch the visual layout anymore**. The 3×3 passed its POC.\n\nThe next build is the **host adapter layer** underneath it:\n\n`Seat Registry`\n→ `surface_type`\n→ appropriate launcher\n→ register PID/HWND\n→ health check\n→ focus/restart\n\nSo instead of one `handleOpencodeSeat()`, conceptually we want something like:\n\n- `handleBrowserSeat()`\n- `handleOpenCodeSeat()`\n- `handleVoiceBridgeSeat()`\n- later maybe `handleNativeSeat()`\n\nAnd the **seat config chooses the handler**. The renderer shouldn't know how Coda launches.\n\nThat means Coda might register:\n\n```text\nseat: Coda\nsurface_type: browser\nbrowser: Brave\nprofile: Peter's authenticated profile\ntarget: ChatGPT\n```\n\nCorrado:\n\n```text\nseat: Corrado\nsurface_type: opencode\nprovider: Moonshot\nmodel: K3-256K\nthinking: low\nmode: YOLO\n```\n\nRagno:\n\n```text\nseat: Ragno\nsurface_type: opencode\nprovider: Moonshot\nmodel: Kimi 2.8 Preview\nmode: YOLO\n```\n\nAnd then Talon/Keel/etc. each get their actual runtime assignments rather than inheriting **Big Pickle OpenCode Zen**, which I can visibly see all over this screenshot. That's the tell: the identity directory changed, but the runtime configuration didn't. They're different identities wearing essentially the same default OpenCode runtime.\n\nSo the current state is:\n\n**Identity routing: PASS.**  \n**3×3 layout: PASS.**  \n**VoiceBridge health integration: PASS for POC.**  \n**Host/surface routing: NOT BUILT.**  \n**Runtime/model binding: NOT YET CONSUMED.**  \n**Coda authenticated Brave surface: NOT BUILT; current iframe/docked approach is the wrong first primitive.**\n\nAnd I would stop exactly there. **Don't polish the UI. Don't build the VoiceBridge queue yet. Don't add more buttons.**\n\nThe next test should be brutally narrow:\n\n**Can the registry launch/focus Coda into Peter's authenticated Brave ChatGPT window, Corrado into K3-256K low/YOLO, and Ragno into Kimi 2.8 Preview/YOLO — each from its stable seat definition?**\n\nIf those three work, we have proved the architecture rather than merely the grid. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1789709088.349443, "end_turn": true, "id": "7052b9dc-aa85-4e01-a972-18106a47938f", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": null, "end_idx": 5591, "invalid": false, "matched_text": "memcite", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": [], "start_idx": 5582, "type": "hidden"}], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "d167898a-657d-4589-a9bc-90500dfb1fc4", "request_id": "62066f6f-15f5-421b-97d3-23bc7b59c6a6", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "1fed9948-ee47-4993-9695-072675f61d2e", "turn_id": "9598de49-2378-4c0d-9eb8-2fd5cc0c9509", "working_turn_id": "1fed9948-ee47-4993-9695-072675f61d2e"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789709120.778271, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content