, "turn_exchange_id": "2e86c25b-522e-48db-848b-c6e09ab1099b", "turn_id": "5b037c83-69aa-4478-a2b9-45efdc6b47a3", "working_turn_id": "2e86c25b-522e-48db-848b-c6e09ab1099b"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790016827.459756, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Give GLM something like this:\n\n> **GLM — architecture challenge only. Do not implement.**\n>\n> Design the architecture for a **mobile executor layer** that acts as the phone-side command surface for GCE/Aegis.\n>\n> The phone is **not the brain**. It is a trusted edge terminal that captures voice/screenshots/events, presents proposed actions, and executes approved commands against external systems.\n>\n> Use this flow as the starting point:\n>\n> `Phone capture → event normalization → state update → Projection / Committee Engine → proposed state / action plan → approval gate → mobile executor → external system mutation → result/evidence → state reconciliation`\n>\n> Requirements:\n>\n> - Separate **capture**, **reasoning/projection**, **approval**, and **execution**.\n> - Executor must be deterministic where possible.\n> - No direct mutation from raw voice intent.\n> - Support reversible vs irreversible action classes.\n> - Preserve `IDENTITY != ROLE != AUTHORITY != MODEL`.\n> - Support multiple adapters: calendar, tasks, email, files, notifications, device actions.\n> - Maintain a small local execution queue with action state: proposed / approved / running / succeeded / failed / rolled back.\n> - Every execution returns evidence and updates canonical state.\n> - Allow pre-authorized low-risk actions, but require explicit approval for external sends, financial commitments, production mutations, destructive actions, or material scope changes.\n> - Mobile UI should stay thin: command queue, approvals, status, exceptions, recent evidence.\n> - Assume Android-class hardware first; do not bind the architecture to one phone vendor.\n> - Treat connectivity loss, stale state, duplicate commands, retries, auth expiration, and conflicting concurrent actions as first-class failure modes.\n>\n> Deliver:\n>\n> 1. component architecture\n> 2. trust and authority boundaries\n> 3. executor state machine\n> 4. adapter/plugin contract\n> 5. approval model\n> 6. sync/reconciliation model\n> 7. failure/retry/idempotency strategy\n> 8. minimum viable prototype\n> 9. what should remain on-device vs remote\n> 10. what assumptions need to be tested before build\n>\n> Keep it lean. Challenge the design where needed. Do not invent a full mobile OS or custom hardware.\n\nThat should force GLM to architect the **executor as a bounded control plane**, instead of accidentally turning the phone into another giant AI runtime."]}, "create_time": 1790016813.746709, "end_turn": true, "id": "f04dc12c-5032-414f-89f5-b7c959955d7a", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "0e0744a1-9c4f-446b-b620-d289b6509f9d", "request_id": "29eaa9d9-4ef9-45e2-ab41-28065e54f880", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "2e86c25b-522e-48db-848b-c6e09ab1099b", "turn_id": "952488b5-9a04-4c01-abe4-e019a5652c0c", "working_turn_id": "2e86c25b-522e-48db-848b-c6e09ab1099b"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790016928.363067, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "model_editable_context", "model_set_context": "", "repo_summary": null, "repository": null, "structured_context": null}, "create_time": 1790016813.7478342, "end_tu