"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content": "Worked for 12s", "content_type": "reasoning_recap"}, "create_time": 1790105226.137872, "end_turn": false, "id": "bccbf40e-67c0-457d-858b-4d4dae52ee7a", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 12, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "44a76db8-562a-47ba-9b4d-e7c8afd560a6", "reasoning_end_time": 1790105226.0988197, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1790105213.2951405, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "d519a463-30f0-48c9-bec9-993c36ccbf92", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "turn_exchange_id": "0aef906e-d8d7-4e4e-a819-1eeed556e38f", "turn_id": "658f13d7-9ea8-4ffc-a09f-36c459000ceb", "working_turn_id": "0aef906e-d8d7-4e4e-a819-1eeed556e38f"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Fresh sandbox — the Season 1 ledger, Process v2 refactor, and the VoiceBridge/Tailscale artifacts aren't in my output folder this session. I'm Kimi, TA seat, grounded off the Walking Capture spec you just dropped. Everything below is built from the spec itself; where the spec says \"inspect existing work,\" I can't see your machine from here — I flag those two checkpoints for you.\r\n\r\nBottom line: the spec is sound and the scope discipline is right. Plan is buildable in one pass. Here's the v0.1 build plan, per §21.\r\n\r\n## 1. Proposed v0.1 implementation\r\n\r\nOne iOS Shortcut named **\"Capture Thought\"** that does: Dictate Text → build capture envelope → append to local JSONL (via Scriptable) → attempt transport → show \"Captured.\" → exit.\r\n\r\nTrigger surfaces all call that one Shortcut:\r\n- **Primary**: Voice Control custom command (\"Take note\") — deterministic, no Siri conversational parsing, works via vocal trigger without unlocking if Voice Control is on. Note: Voice Control requires Settings → Accessibility → Voice Control enabled; that's a one-time setup cost Peter pays once.\r\n- **Secondary**: Action Button → Shortcuts → Capture Thought (instant, screen on).\r\n- **Tertiary**: Lock Screen / Home Screen Shortcut icon as manual fallback.\r\n\r\n## 2. Shortcuts vs Scriptable split\r\n\r\n**Shortcuts owns**: triggers, Dictate Text (native mic UI, auto-stops when Peter stops talking), haptic/confirmation feedback.\r\n**Scriptable owns**: envelope construction (UUID, ISO-8601 timestamp with tz, schema_version), JSON serialization, local file append to queue, transport attempt + state write, retry-on-next-capture.\r\n\r\nSplit follows §6 exactly: Shortcuts where it's more reliable (dictation, triggers), Scriptable only where it materially improves (envelope, queue, transport).\r\n\r\n## 3. Selected transport: Google Drive (with checkpoint), Tailscale as plan B\r\n\r\n**Checkpoint for you first**: is the prior Tailscale receiver still running on the Razer, and what's its endpoint? If yes, it's the better long-term path (direct into GCE, survives Android switch, no third-party dependency) — reuse it per §11.\r\n\r\nIf it's dead or annoying: **Google Drive via Shortcuts' native \"Append to File\"** action. No OAuth machinery, no API keys, works from Shortcuts natively, cross-platform. Files land in `GCE_DON/capture-inbox/walking/<date>/captures.jsonl`, and a desktop-side sync client (Drive for desktop or rclone on the Razer) delivers to local disk. Drive append is the known-fragile piece (concurrent appends can race on rapid successive captures), which is why Scriptable keeps the local queue as truth and Drive is just a pipe.\r\n\r\nIf both are messy: local-only per §10-C, manual AirDrop at end of walk. Don't block the POC.\r\n\r\n## 4. Local storage method\r\n\r\nScriptable writes to its own Documents directory: `walking-capture/queue/captures.jsonl` — one JSON object per line, immutable, `transport_state: pending|synced`. Daily human view `daily.md` rendered by Scriptable on each capture (append a `## HH:MM` block). Retention: keep local copies 30 days even after synced (§14 Rule 2). Dedup key = `capture_id` everywhere downstream.\r\n\r\n## 5. Desktop receiver/destination\r\n\r\nA deliberately dumb watcher script on the Razer (Python, ~80 lines, runs as a scheduled task): watches the inbox folder → dedups by capture_id → persists to the canonical capture store → re-renders `daily.md` → emits the tiny status view (Today / Synced / Pending / Failed / Last capture) as a text file you can glance at.\r\n\r\n**Checkpoint two**: exact canonical path — spec §12 says reconcile against current GCE filesystem authority before materializing. Tell me the current GCE root on the Razer and I'll slot the inbox under it instead of inventing a parallel structure.\r\n\r\n## 6. Files/scripts to be created\r\n\r\n- iOS Shortcut \"Capture Thought\" (built on-device, I'll give you exact step-by-step)\r\n- `walking-capture.js` — Scriptable capture function (envelope, local queue, transport attempt)\r\n- `capture_receiver.py` — desktop watcher/dedup/daily renderer\r\n- `STATUS.md` — the 5-line diagnostics view, regenerated by the receiver\r\n- Nothing else. No GCE canon touched, no Notion writes, no Command Center coupling.\r\n\r\n## 7. Rollback / removal\r\n\r\nEverything lives in three isolated spots: the Shortcut (delete it), Scriptable documents folder (delete `walking-capture/`), inbox folder on desktop (archive, don't delete — captures are evidence). No system files, no registries, no canonical GCE mutation, so removal is total and clean.\r\n\r\n## 8. End-to-end test plan\r\n\r\n1. Desk test: 5 captures via icon trigger, 1 via Voice Control phrase — verify envelope fields, UUID uniqueness, local JSONL append.\r\n2. Rapid-fire test: 3 captures within 30 seconds — no loss, no interleaved JSON corruption.\r\n3. Long ramble: 3+ minute dictation — Dictate Text's own limit is the risk; verify it survives.\r\n4. Airplane mode walk: 5 captures offline — all land locally with `pending`, UI still says \"Captured.\"\r\n5. Reconnect — transport retries quietly on next capture or on a Scriptable run-on-open hook; nothing lost.\r\n6. Accidental trigger/cancel — cancel produces no envelope (or an explicitly-marked-cancelled one; I'll make cancel produce nothing).\r\n7. Desktop: inbox receives, dedups, `daily.md` chronological, STATUS.txt correct counts.\r\n8. Then the real acceptance test from §19 — the 20-thought walk.\r\n\r\n## Known platform limitation to flag now\r\n\r\nVoice Control as the hands-free trigger means Voice Control stays on, which changes some touch behavior on the phone. Action Button is the zero-friction alternative but requires the phone in hand / screen awake. That's the one real trade-off in the design — no architecture creep needed to solve it, just your pick of primary trigger.\r\n\r\nTwo things I need from you before build: **(a)** Tailscale receiver status/endpoint on the Razer, **(b)** current GCE root path on the Razer for inbox placement. Give me those and I deliver the Shortcut steps + Scriptable script + receiver script."]}, "create_time": 1790105509.93, "end_turn": null, "id": "ce1a8961-4858-4580-98a1-f4bf022ba2f4", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "33e9417f-c56a-4e7c-b6fb-caf3a9cac649", "turn_exchange_id": "c117c19a-6ea8-484a-8c09-78c9a857fc8e", "turn_id": "f2e20a80-cc44-4ac6-aed3-3cd02cd07ce1", "working_turn_id": "c117c19a-6ea8-484a-8c09-78c9a857fc8e"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790105541.231627, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "code", "language