rking_turn_id": "344087cf-3460-4d25-9f63-8a40ce466b47"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790108439.582049, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Exactly. We drifted.\n\nYou said **prove the phone capture behavior first**. The contamination happened because prior Tailscale/VoiceBridge work kept getting pulled forward as if transport had to be part of v0.1.\n\nIt doesn’t.\n\nFor the first POC, the whole architecture can live on the iPhone:\n\n**Trigger → Dictate → Timestamp → Save locally → Done**\n\nThat’s it.\n\nNo Razer.  \nNo Tailscale.  \nNo VoiceBridge.  \nNo GCE inbox.  \nNo receiver.  \nNo desktop daemon.  \nNo transport architecture.\n\nUse **Shortcuts + Scriptable + local Files/Notes storage** and prove the interaction loop.\n\nThe cleanest v0.1 is probably:\n\n**Shortcut trigger**\n→ **Dictate Text**\n→ **Scriptable creates immutable capture**\n→ save under something like:\n\n`On My iPhone/Scriptable/WalkingCapture/raw/YYYY-MM-DD/<capture_id>.json`\n\nand derive:\n\n`daily.md`\n\nor even append to one Apple Note if we want the human-facing version immediately.\n\nThen when you finish the walk, **you manually open/export/share the daily capture**. That manual handoff is perfectly acceptable for a POC because the thing we are testing is:\n\n> **Will Peter naturally dump thoughts this way without breaking stride?**\n\nTransport is a separate problem.\n\nSo I’d reset the build spec to:\n\n> **PHONE-ONLY POC.**\n>\n> Build nothing off-device.\n>\n> Required:\n> - one trigger\n> - dictation\n> - timestamp\n> - immutable local storage\n> - chronological daily view\n> - tiny capture/status confirmation\n>\n> Explicitly prohibited for v0.1:\n> - Tailscale\n> - VoiceBridge\n> - Google Drive\n> - desktop receiver\n> - GCE routing\n> - AI classification\n> - automatic sync\n>\n> At the end of the walk, Don manually reviews or