n_sec": 1, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "ae09b3e7-b5f2-4f0b-b949-c6c9c6e58de7", "reasoning_end_time": 1790113827.415306, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1790113826.0278406, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "837930bb-aaf7-4a79-bbea-13522965c52e", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "turn_exchange_id": "b4bbad2a-0d2a-4627-bac5-f5b998742eec", "turn_id": "c9b18908-9ff2-4acb-94d1-f94463904f5f", "working_turn_id": "b4bbad2a-0d2a-4627-bac5-f5b998742eec"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Adopted. The capture path is now a single write, and `daily.md` is nobody's business until review time. Capture writes evidence; review renders evidence. Here's the whole build — two scripts, one shortcut, nothing else.\r\n\r\n## Storage\r\n\r\n```\r\nOn My iPhone/Scriptable/WalkingCapture/\r\n  2026-09-22/\r\n    a1b2…e9.json     ← written ONLY at capture time, never rewritten\r\n    daily.md         ← written ONLY by review.js, always rebuildable\r\n```\r\n\r\n## capture.js\r\n\r\nPaste into Scriptable, name it exactly `capture` (the shortcut references it by name):\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\n// capture.js — Walking Capture v0.1 (phone-only)\r\n// Called by the \"Capture Thought\" shortcut. Parameter format:\r\n//   line 1 = trigger source (passed by the shortcut, not assumed here)\r\n//   rest   = raw dictated text\r\n// Returns to shortcut: \"ok\" | \"cancelled\" | \"fail\"\r\n// Writes EXACTLY ONE immutable file. Touches nothing else.\r\n\r\nconst FM = FileManager.local()\r\nconst ROOT = FM.joinPath(FM.documentsDirectory(), \"WalkingCapture\")\r\n\r\nfunction finish(result) {\r\n  Script.setShortcutOutput(result)\r\n  Script.complete()\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction pad(n) { return (n < 10 ? \"0\" : \"\") + n }\r\n\r\nfunction uuid4() {\r\n  const hex = \"0123456789abcdef\"\r\n  let s = \"\"\r\n  for (let i = 0; i < 36; i++) {\r\n    if (i === 8 || i === 13 || i === 18 || i === 23) s += \"-\"\r\n    else if (i === 14) s += \"4\"\r\n    else if (i === 19) s += \"89ab\"[Math.floor(Math.random() * 4)]\r\n    else s += hex[Math.floor(Math.random() * 16)]\r\n  }\r\n  return s\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction isoLocal(d) {\r\n  const off = d.getTimezoneOffset()   // minutes west of UTC\r\n  const sign = off <= 0 ? \"+\" : \"-\"\r\n  const a = Math.abs(off)\r\n  return d.getFullYear() + \"-\" + pad(d.getMonth() + 1) + \"-\" + pad(d.getDate()) +\r\n    \"T\" + pad(d.getHours()) + \":\" + pad(d.getMinutes()) + \":\" + pad(d.getSeconds()) +\r\n    sign + pad(Math.floor(a / 60)) + \":\" + pad(a % 60)\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction tzName() {\r\n  try { return Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone || null }\r\n  catch (e) { return null }\r\n}\r\n\r\ntry {\r\n  // Unpack trigger + raw text\r\n  let trigger = \"unknown\"\r\n  let rawText = \"\"\r\n  const p = args.shortcutParameter\r\n  if (typeof p === \"string\") {\r\n    const nl = p.indexOf(\"\\n\")\r\n    trigger = (nl === -1 ? p : p.slice(0, nl)).trim()\r\n    rawText = nl === -1 ? \"\" : p.slice(nl + 1)\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  // Empty guard — never create an empty capture object\r\n  if (rawText.trim().length === 0) finish(\"cancelled\")\r\n\r\n  // Envelope\r\n  const now = new Date()\r\n  const captureId = uuid4()\r\n  const envelope = {\r\n    capture_id: captureId,\r\n    captured_at: isoLocal(now),\r\n    source: \"iphone\",\r\n    capture_type: \"voice\",\r\n    raw_text: rawText,\r\n    timezone: tzName(),\r\n    trigger: trigger,\r\n    schema_version: \"0.1\"\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  // The single write: WalkingCapture/<YYYY-MM-DD>/<capture_id>.json\r\n  const dayDir = FM.joinPath(ROOT,\r\n    now.getFullYear() + \"-\" + pad(now.getMonth() + 1) + \"-\" + pad(now.getDate()))\r\n  if (!FM.isDirectory(dayDir)) FM.createDirectory(dayDir, true)\r\n  const path = FM.joinPath(dayDir, captureId + \".json\")\r\n  FM.writeString(path, JSON.stringify(envelope, null, 2))  // no overwrite: a collision fails rather than clobbers\r\n\r\n  // Success = the file exists on-device\r\n  finish(FM.fileExists(path) ? \"ok\" : \"fail\")\r\n} catch (e) {\r\n  finish(\"fail\")\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe empty guard lives in the script, not the shortcut — one implementation, not two places that can disagree.\r\n\r\n## The shortcut — exact steps\r\n\r\n1. Shortcuts → **+** → rename **Capture Thought**\r\n2. Add action **Dictate Text** → Stop Listening: **After Pause**\r\n3. Add action **Text** → type `action_button`, tap return, then insert the **Dictated Text** variable on the second line\r\n4. Add action **Run Scriptable Script** → Script: `capture` → tap **Parameter** and insert the **Text** output → Show When Run **off**\r\n5. Add action **If**: **Script Result is ok** → **Show Notification** \"Captured.\" (leave Play Sound on — that's the audible confirm while walking; add a vibrate action too if your Shortcuts has one)\r\n6. **Otherwise If**: Script Result is cancelled → Show Notification \"Cancelled.\"\r\n7. **Otherwise** → Show Notification \"Capture failed.\"\r\n\r\nLine 1 of that Text action is the trigger protocol Coda asked for: a second trigger surface later means its wrapper writes its own name on line 1. The script never assumes Action Button.\r\n\r\nBind it: **Settings → Action Button → Shortcut → Capture Thought.** Back Tap is a free second binding to the same shortcut if you want a pocket fallback — a Settings toggle, not a build.\r\n\r\n## review.js — the Review Today operation\r\n\r\nPaste into Scriptable, name it `review`. Run it from the Scriptable app after the walk (or wrap in a one-action \"Review Today\" shortcut with Show When Run **on** — it needs the screen):\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\n// review.js — Walking Capture v0.1\r\n// Reads today's immutable capture objects, regenerates daily.md (derived view),\r\n// presents it. Raw JSON files are the authority; daily.md is disposable.\r\n\r\nconst FM = FileManager.local()\r\nconst ROOT = FM.joinPath(FM.documentsDirectory(), \"WalkingCapture\")\r\n\r\nfunction pad(n) { return (n < 10 ? \"0\" : \"\") + n }\r\n\r\nfunction clockTime(d) {\r\n  let h = d.getHours()\r\n  const ap = h >= 12 ? \"PM\" : \"AM\"\r\n  h = h % 12; if (h === 0) h = 12\r\n  return h + \":\" + pad(d.getMinutes()) + \" \" + ap\r\n}\r\n\r\n(async function() {\r\n  const now = new Date()\r\n  const day = now.getFullYear() + \"-\" + pad(now.getMonth() + 1) + \"-\" + pad(now.getDate())\r\n  const dayDir = FM.joinPath(ROOT, day)\r\n\r\n  let captures = []\r\n  if (FM.isDirectory(dayDir)) {\r\n    for (const name of FM.listDirectory(dayDir)) {\r\n      if (!name.endsWith(\".json\")) continue\r\n      try {\r\n        const env = JSON.parse(FM.readString(FM.joinPath(dayDir, name)))\r\n        if (env && env.raw_text) captures.push(env)\r\n      } catch (e) { /* unreadable file: skip it, never touch it */ }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  captures.sort((a, b) => new Date(a.captured_at) - new Date(b.captured_at))\r\n\r\n  if (captures.length === 0) {\r\n    await QuickLook.present(\"Walking Capture — \" + day + \"\\n\\nNo captures yet.\")\r\n    return\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  let md = \"# Walking Capture — \" + day + \"\\n\\n\"\r\n  for (const c of captures) {\r\n    const t = new Date(c.captured_at)\r\n    md += \"## \" + (isNaN(t) ? c.captured_at : clockTime(t)) + \"\\n\" + c.raw_text.trim() + \"\\n\\n\"\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const mdPath = FM.joinPath(dayDir, \"daily.md\")\r\n  FM.writeString(mdPath, md, true)   // derived view: always safe to overwrite\r\n  await QuickLook.present(mdPath, true)\r\n})()\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Bench test — 15 minutes, before any walk\r\n\r\n1. Run Capture Thought once **from inside the Shortcuts app** to clear the mic-permission prompt — not mid-walk.\r\n2. Action Button with screen **locked** — press, speak. Record the verdict: dictation straight away, or iOS demands unlock first? Whatever the answer, that's the ceiling, not a bug.\r\n3. Happy path: file exists in Files → On My iPhone → Scriptable → WalkingCapture → today → one `<uuid>.json`. Open it, check the envelope.\r\n4. Three captures in 30 seconds → three distinct IDs.\r\n5. Two-minute ramble with natural pauses. If After Pause truncates it, note where — report, don't patch.\r\n6. Accidental trigger → cancel dictation → **no new file** (either \"Cancelled.\" or a silent stop — both pass).\r\n7. Open Scriptable → tap `review` → the day's note presents, chronological.\r\n\r\nTwo install notes: running `capture` directly from the Scriptable app returns \"cancelled\" (no parameter passed) — expected, test through the shortcut. And captures always land in on-device storage even if Scriptable syncs scripts through iCloud.\r\n\r\nThat's the build. Stopping here per instructions.\r\n\r\nWalk first. Twenty thoughts minimum. When you've got 20–50 real capture objects sitting in dated folders, we open them up, look at what Peter actually produces, and design the compiler from evidence instead of imagination."]}, "create_time": 1790132224.453, "end_turn": null, "id": "e4edb677-bd3e-48e2-a926-aecf055af125", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "3d116476-2118-45d2-9b48-0971197a14a7", "turn_exchange_id": "a3fb7040-d5e5-4713-b58a-064d1a2a12e2", "turn_id": "05fdf605-4cdf-483e-ae3f-2caf894466f7", "working_turn_id": "a3fb7040-d5e5-4713-b58a-064d1a2a12e2"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790132246.543105, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["This is finally at the right altitude. **Phone-only, one capture write, one derived review surface.** I’d install it after **two tiny code corrections**—nothing architectural.\n\n### 1. Make `finish()` actually terminate the caller path\n\nRight now:\n\n```javascript\nif (rawText.trim().length === 0) finish(\"cancelled\")\n```\n\nI would change it to:\n\n```javascript\nif (rawText.trim().length === 0) {\n  finish(\"cancelled\")\n  return\n}\n```\n\nAnd ideally make every terminal `finish()` followed by `return`. Don’t rely on `Script.complete()` implicitly preventing subsequent JavaScript from running. The semantic rule should be explicit: **terminal state means stop execution.**\n\n### 2. The UUID collision comment is currently false\n\nThis line:\n\n```javascript\nFM.writeString(path, JSON.stringify(envelope, null, 2))\n```\n\nwill normally overwrite an existing file at that path. The comment says a collision fails rather than clobbers, but the code doesn’t enforce that.\n\nBefore writing:\n\n```javascript\nif (FM.fileExists(path)) {\n  finish(\"fail\")\n  return\n}\n```\n\nThen write and verify.\n\nThat preserves the doctrine we actually care about:\n\n> **A capture object, once written, is immutable.**\n\nEverything else looks appropriately boring—which is exactly what v0.1 should be.\n\nI especially like that we ended up with:\n\n```text\nCAPTURE\nAction Button\n→ Dictation\n→ immutable JSON\n→ confirmation\n\nREVIEW\nimmutable JSON objects\n→ derive daily.md\n→ display\n```\n\nNo transport state, no GCE knowledge, no AI, no Tailscale, no VoiceBridge, no classification.\n\nAnd I would **not add another thing before the walk**. Even the “Review Today” wrapper can remain optional because `review.js` already gives you what you need.\n\nSo the gate is now:\n\n**Fix those two lines → install → permissions bench test → real 20-thought walk.**\n\nThen we stop theorizing and inspect what Peter actually produces. That corpus becomes the design input for Layer 2."]}, "create_time": 1790132226.776333, "end_turn": true, "id": "04c0f2e3-b206-473e-b5f2-1dd654d84868", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "4igx78", "preview_language": null, "preview