```javascript\nconst p = args.shortcutParameter\n\nif (typeof p === \"string\") {\n  const nl = p.indexOf(\"\\n\")\n\n  trigger = (nl === -1 ? p : p.slice(0, nl)).trim()\n  rawText = nl === -1 ? \"\" : p.slice(nl + 1)\n}\n```\n\nwith something that accepts either a string **or** Scriptable’s structured shortcut payload:\n\n```javascript\nconst p = args.shortcutParameter\n\nlet packed = \"\"\n\nif (typeof p === \"string\") {\n  packed = p\n} else if (p && Array.isArray(p.texts) && p.texts.length > 0) {\n  packed = String(p.texts[0])\n}\n\nconst nl = packed.indexOf(\"\\n\")\n\ntrigger = (nl === -1 ? packed : packed.slice(0, nl)).trim()\nrawText = nl === -1 ? \"\" : packed.slice(nl + 1)\n```\n\nThen the wiring becomes dead simple:\n\n**Text block**\n```text\naction_button\n[Dictated Text]\n```\n\n↓  \n\n**Run GCE_Capture**\n\nUnder **Texts**:\n- **Add New Item**\n- choose the yellow **Text** variable\n\nThat’s it.\n\nAnd separately, the red **“Dictation is not supported in Siri”** message is still its own issue. We don’t touch that until the Scriptable input is correctly wired.\n\nYou were right to call bullshit on the loop. This is the cleaner path."]}, "create_time": 1790133520.29661, "end_turn": true, "id": "034e93e3-ac5e-4914-838b-f73e2dec5ffe", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "wf7zdh", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "i68hbe", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "ed71eq", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [{"alt": "", "end_idx": 1875, "has_images": false, "matched_text": " ", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": [], "sources": [], "start_idx": 1874, "type": "sources_footnote"}], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "is_