Text block** (the block that literally contains `action_button`) — **not** \"Dictated Text,\" not \"Shortcut Input.\" If you pass Dictated Text directly, the script eats the first line of the thought as the trigger name.\r\n\r\n**Proof you got it right:** tap the inserted pill → **Reveal Action** → it should jump to the Text block showing `action_button`. If it jumps to Dictate Text, clear it and redo.\r\n\r\nAlso: tap the little arrow on the Scriptable action and set **Show When Run → off**.\r\n\r\n## 2. Add the notifications — three flat Ifs\r\n\r\nDon't fight with nested Otherwise-If branches. Add three separate If actions after the Scriptable action, same motion three times:\r\n\r\n- Tap the If's first field → select the Scriptable action's output (labeled \"Script Result\" or \"GCE_Capture Output\")\r\n- Operator: **is** → value: `ok` (no stray spaces)\r\n\r\n| If value is | Add inside |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `ok` | Show Notification: **Captured.** — leave Play Sound **on**, that's your audible confirm while walking |\r\n| `cancelled` | Show Notification: **Cancelled.** |\r\n| `fail` | Show Notification: **Capture failed.** |\r\n\r\nLeave the Otherwise sections empty. Final shape:\r\n\r\n```\r\nDictate Text (After Pause)\r\nText:  action_button ↵ [Dictated Text]\r\nRun GCE_Capture  Parameter: [Text Output]\r\nIf Script Result is \"ok\"        → Captured.\r\nIf Script Result is \"cancelled\" → Cancelled.\r\nIf Script Result is \"fail\"      → Capture failed.\r\n```\r\n\r\n## 3. First run — from the play button, not Siri\r\n\r\nOpen Shortcuts → tap **▶** on Capture Thought → speak a line → expect \"Captured.\"\r\n\r\n- If iOS prompts about speech or running scripts, allow. (If a banner blocks scripts: Settings → Shortcuts → Advanced → Allow Running Scripts.)\r\n- Verify in Files → On My iPhone → Scriptable → **WalkingCapture** → today's folder → one `.json`. Open it: `raw_text` = what you said, `trigger` = `action_button`.\r\n- Don't test by tapping the script inside Scriptable itself — it returns \"cancelled\" with no parameter. By design. Test through the shortcut only.\r\n\r\n## 4. Bind and do the lock test\r\n\r\nSettings → Action Button → Shortcut → Capture Thought. Then press it with the screen **locked** and just record what happens: dictation starts, or iOS demands Face ID first. Either answer is the ceiling, not a bug — that's bench test E0 and we write the verdict down.\r\n\r\nTwo settings ChatGPT already flagged, both correct: **Enable Dictation** on (Settings → General → Keyboard), and **Voice Control off** if you turned it on during earlier experiments (Settings → Accessibility → Voice Control) — Apple blocks standard dictation while it's active.\r\n\r\nOne cleanup note: the script being named `GCE_Capture` instead of `capture` is fine. The shortcut points at whatever script you picked in the list — name is cosmetic. Just confirm the full capture.js is actually pasted in there.\r\n\r\nThat's the entire remaining build. When the play-button run gives you \"Captured.\" and a JSON in the folder, you're done — bind the button and take the walk."]}, "create_time": 1790137076.525, "end_turn": null, "id": "55fb9004-2c29-458f-a57f-1c39e7a0190b", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "9264bf57-01f1-4dd9-8c95-b32f041181f4", "turn_exchange_id": "25f96e7b-f686-48d5-a99f-df8d266fd3f5", "working_turn_id": "25f96e7b-f686-48d5-a99f-df8d266fd3f5"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790137096.306003, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": [""]}, "create_time": 1790137079.878124, "end_turn": false, "id": "83600e32-97d3-4f5e-ae55-402df4200c1f", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "citations": [], "classifier_response": "default", "content_references": [], "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "disable_turn_actions": true, "fini