hat began as a broader GCE Stack brainstorming / architecture sandbox, then narrowed into a concrete iPhone **Walking Capture v0.1** proof of concept.\n\nThe practical goal became:\n\n> Allow Don to press the iPhone Action Button while walking, capture a thought with minimal interruption, preserve it locally, and review/process it later rather than immediately sending every thought to AI.\n\nThe original implementation candidate was:\n\n**Action Button → Dictate Text → Scriptable → immutable JSON**\n\n## Major pivots\n\nThe Dictate Text path created repeated Shortcuts / Scriptable wiring problems and exposed an architectural issue: dictated text was being treated as “raw” evidence even though Apple dictation is already an interpretation layer.\n\nThe chat pivoted to:\n\n**Action Button → Record Audio → Save File**\n\nThis was successfully bench-tested on the actual phone.\n\nThe key conceptual correction was then ratified:\n\n> **Audio is the authority. Transcription is a derived projection.**\n\nThe earlier Dictate Text design was **not proven broken overall**. It was superseded before its non-Siri execution path was fully tested because audio-first was judged a better primitive on doctrine and implementation simplicity.\n\n## Final scope\n\nThe surviving v0.1 scope is deliberately small:\n\n**Action Button → Record Audio → unique local audio file → confirmation**\n\nTranscription, JSON, daily summaries, AI classification, desktop transport, VoiceBridge, Tailscale, network synchronization, and downstream reconciliation remain outside the capture critical path.\n\n---\n\n# 3. ACCOMPLISHMENTS BY DATE\n\n## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n**WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \nWalking Capture v0.1 was scoped as a phone-only POC. Initial architecture used iPhone Shortcuts with Dictate Text feeding Scriptable, intended to create immutable JSON captures.\n\n**DECISION / RESULT:**  \nPhone-only scope was locked. Network, desktop, VoiceBridge, Tailscale, Drive, AI classification, and background processing were explicitly excluded from v0.1.\n\n**WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don authority; Coda design/support.\n\n**STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n**WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \nA Scriptable capture implementation named `GCE_Capture` was developed to receive shortcut text and write immutable JSON under a WalkingCapture directory.\n\n**DECISION / RESULT:**  \nThe implementation included UUID capture IDs, local timestamps, source/capture metadata, overwrite protection, and terminal statuses such as `ok`, `cancelled`, and `fail`.\n\n**WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Coda implementation support under Don direction.\n\n**STATUS:** implemented, later superseded from the capture critical path\n\n---\n\n## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n**WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \nActual iPhone Shortcuts behavior was pressure-tested through screenshots and live interaction.\n\n**DECISION / RESULT:**  \nSeveral assumed Shortcuts / Scriptable input behaviors were disproven by the actual UI:\n- Scriptable’s visible `Parameter` field opened a file picker.\n- Scriptable’s `Texts` editor did not behave like a normal persistent literal-text field.\n- The intended Dictate Text → composed Text → Scriptable parameter path was not successfully proven.\n\nA Siri-context banner explicitly showed:\n\n**“Dictation is not supported in Siri.”**\n\n**WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don performed ground test; Coda reconciled findings.\n\n**STATUS:** verified\n\n---\n\n## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n**WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \nDon identified that `Dictate Text` itself was the wrong primitive for the desired capture behavior.\n\n**DECISION / RESULT:**  \nThe design pivoted from text-first capture to **Record Audio**.\n\n**WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don identified the break; Coda formulated the architectural pivot.\n\n**STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n**WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \nNative Shortcuts `Record Audio` was added and executed successfully.\n\n**DECISION / RESULT:**  \nThe ph